/-!
# Small matrices for the mixed-extension upper bound

The rows record sixteen scalar consequences of five explicit word relations
on x₀₁(1), x₀₁(ω), and the cyclic coordinate permutation. The 27-by-11
matrix consists of the two proposed mixed blocks followed by the nine section
changes. The projection and recovery matrices give the explicit elimination
identity checked in `Certificate`.

These are concrete coefficient arrays, not assumed cocycle equations or a
classification. `Certificate` proves their relation to the actual group words
and checks their elimination identity in the Lean kernel. Source context:
James (1973), Lemma 8.3; Aschbacher–Smith H.12.1, printed pp.393–394.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

